## Upstream reference: webview-kiosk

This project was designed after inspecting **webview-kiosk** by nktnet1:

- Repository: https://github.com/nktnet1/webview-kiosk
- License: AGPL-3.0-or-later

No source files from webview-kiosk were copied into this repository. The
following *architectural patterns* were adopted because they are proven in that
project:

- Declaring a HOME/DEFAULT intent filter so the app can act as the device
  launcher, together with a "kiosk control panel" that is behind an adult gate.
- Blocking navigation at the WebView layer with an explicit allow-list, rather
  than relying on hiding browser chrome.
- Keeping a recovery path out of kiosk mode (service-side unlock, settings PIN)
  so a child can never be trapped in an inaccessible screen.

Because the reference project and this project are both AGPL-3.0-or-later, the
strong-copyleft source-sharing obligations apply consistently: if you run a
modified version of this software as a network service or distribute APKs built
from it, you must make the corresponding source available under the same licence.

